  {
    "shortcode": "DKjftTRsBYI",
    "caption": "Losing at a freediving competition hits harder than you’d expect. You trained for months, maybe years, sacrificed weekends, pushed through injuries, skipped celebrations, only to come up early, black out, or forget a surface protocol. It feels unfair. Frustrating. Like all that effort vanished in a couple of minutes. But here’s the truth: losing doesn’t mean you’re not good enough. It just means you have more to learn. And the people who keep showing up after they lose? They’re the ones who eventually go the deepest.\n⠀\n🧜🏻‍♀️ @silvia_freediving \n📸 @kostek_visuals \n⠀\n#alchemy #alchemyfins #freediving #alchemyv3 #underwaterphotography #freedive #carbon #carbonfins #bifins #diving #ocean #nature #fitness #explore #freedivingphotos #watersports #discover #adventure #saltlife #apnea #freediver #freediverlife #freedivingfins",
